<title>TURKEY: Turkish 13-mth bond yield jumps to 114.71 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish 13-mth bond yield jumps to 114.71 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield in the Turkish Treasury's 399-day bond auction rose to 114.71 percent on Tuesday from 106.77 percent in the previous 399-day bond auction on March 18.</p>
<p>	Maturity		    : April 29, 1998</p>
<p>	Amount			: 344.5 trln lira</p>
<p>	Bid amount		  : 377.3 trln lira</p>
<p>	Maximum yield	     : 114.71</p>
<p>	Lowest accepted price   : 43,275 lira</p>
<p>	Payment date		: March 26, 1997</p>
<p>Banks will pay 145.6 trillion lira to the Treasury for the auction on Wednesday when they will cash in 189.3 trillion lira from maturing t-bills. -- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
</text>
